            <div xml:id="d427">

                <pb facs="0531" n="459" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg459"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6369/510.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Heimke to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-12-26"><hi rendition="#italic">December 26,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Heimke says the commander of the United States cruiser <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Albany</hi> telegraphs from Corinto that Zelaya left
                    there on Friday for Salina Cruz on a Mexican warship. Mr. Heimke states that he
                    has telegraphed this information to the embassy at Mexico.</p>
            </div>
